Source: parakeet-cpp
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ronny Rentner <debian@ronny-rentner.de>
Homepage: https://github.com/mudler/parakeet.cpp
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
               cmake,
               git,
               glslc,
               libvulkan-dev

Package: parakeet-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: NVIDIA Parakeet speech recognition command line tool
 parakeet-cli transcribes WAV files with NVIDIA NeMo Parakeet models
 converted to GGUF, running on the CPU or a Vulkan GPU through ggml.

Package: parakeet-server
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: curl
Description: NVIDIA Parakeet speech recognition HTTP server
 parakeet-server answers POST /v1/audio/transcriptions like the OpenAI
 API, with phrase boosting, model selection per request and unloading of
 idle models.
